In the poll, more than 63 percent of those residents with opinions said the city should not build the project. Opposition is slightly higher — 65 percent — among registered voters. While nearly three-fourths of residents believe traffic needs to be reduced on highways around downtown, only 17 percent of those people believe building Trinity Parkway is the right way to relieve traffic.
The results shed light on how residents and voters view the project on the eve of elections that will seat the City Council members who decide the project��s fate. The project itself is not on the ballot, but 65 percent of registered voters say where candidates stand on the issue is an important consideration in whom they vote for.
